# mutgap_disp_mapper_texture_refused_dies: A mapped BGRA surface 16400 pixels wide, over the 16384-texel limit: the IOSurface host device maps it (nothing limits a descriptor's width), and opcode 8 asks Metal for a texture on it. Metal's own descriptor validation aborts the host inside newTextureWithDescriptor:iosurface: ("width (16400) greater than the maximum allowed size of 16384"), with MTL_DEBUG_LAYER unset, so the call never returns nil and the library's own death on a nil texture is never reached; a bytesPerRow not aligned to 16 and a height of 16400 abort the same way. A guest kills the host with one descriptor. Map and isolate only: the mapper needs a memory map.
